        {
          "id": "60cccf27d58b22da6990a017",
          "questionNumber": 1,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "If it is possible to make a meaningful word with the second, fourth, fifth, and eighth letters of the word \"REGARDING\" which of the following will be the second letter from the right end of that newly formed word? If more than one such word can be made, give M as the answer and if no such word can be made, give Y as the answer.",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "R",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "A",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "Y",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "N",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "M",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "5",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p>The second, fourth, fifth, and eighth&nbsp;letters of the word \"REGARDING\" are E, A, R, and N&nbsp;respectively&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Meaningful words can be formed&nbsp;&rarr; EARN, NEAR, REAN, and NARE</p>\n\n<p>Hence,<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">&nbsp;the correct answer is M as more than 1 word can be formed.</span></p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
        {
          "id": "6079767e663c800aae757975",
          "questionNumber": 2,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p dir=\"ltr\">How many pairs of letters are there in the word<strong>&nbsp;\"CONSISTENCY\"&nbsp;</strong>each of which have as many letters between them in the word as they have between them in the English alphabetical series?</p>",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "Five",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "Four",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "Two",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "Three",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "More than five",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "5",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/21/06/F1_Shraddha_Kanchan_17.06.2021_D1.png\" style=\"height: 121px; width: 499px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>There are six&nbsp;pairs</p>\n\n<p>Hence, there are<strong> more than five pairs.</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong>Alternate Method:</strong></p>\n\n<p>We can use the place values of the letters and then we can find how many letters are there in between the letters. <strong>(we can use this method only when we remember all the letters place values)</strong></p>\n\n<p><strong><img src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImage2.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 50px;\" /></strong></p>\n\n<p>When nothing specific about forward or backward is given in the question, we have to take both directions,&nbsp;</p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
        {
          "id": "6079637dd29f53f0bbd1af98",
          "questionNumber": 3,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "If it is possible to make a meaningful word with the first, third, and eighth letters of the word \"PREDOMINANT\" which of the following will be the second letter from the right end of that newly formed word? If more than one such word can be made, give M as the answer and if no such word can be made, give Y as the answer.",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "P",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "N",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "E",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "M",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "Y",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "3",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p>The first, third, and eighth letters of the word PREDOMINANT are P, E, and N respectively.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>1st&nbsp;letter&nbsp;&rarr; P,&nbsp; &nbsp;3rd&nbsp;letter&nbsp;&rarr; E, and 8th&nbsp;letter&nbsp;&rarr; N</p>\n\n<p>So, PEN is a meaningful word.</p>\n\n<p>Hence,<strong> E is the second letter from the right end.</strong></p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
        {
          "id": "60548cec56e12ce026ef8def",
          "questionNumber": 4,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p><strong>Directions:</strong> Study the following information carefully to answer the given questions:</p>\n\n<p>4 7 @ J # 9 P $ L % O &copy; 5 &amp; G C W D 3 8 @ S # 1 F Y V&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>How many letters are there in the English alphabetical series which come&nbsp;in between the element which is nineteenth from the right end and the element which is fifteenth from the left end in the above arrangement?</p>",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "Two",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "Five",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "Six",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "Four",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "None of the above",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "4",
          "marks": 1,
          "negativeMarks": 0.25,
          "explanation": "<p><strong>Given arrangement:</strong> 4 7 @ J # 9 P $ L % O &copy; 5 &amp; G C W D 3 8 @ S # 1 F Y V</p>\n\n<p>Element which is 19<sup>th</sup> from the right end in the above arrangement: <strong>L</strong></p>\n\n<p>Element which is 15<sup>th</sup> from the left end in the above arrangement:<strong> G</strong></p>\n\n<p>In English alphabet, the letters which come in between L and G:</p>\n\n<p>A B C D E F G <strong>H I J K</strong> L M N O P Q R S T U V W X Y Z</p>\n\n<p>Hence,<strong> there are four letters (i.e. H, I, J, K) which come in between the element which is nineteenth from the right end and the element which is fifteenth from the left end in the above arrangement.</strong></p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
        {
          "id": "605489d24cfbdca1bade5471",
          "questionNumber": 5,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p><strong>Directions:</strong> Study the following information carefully to answer the given questions:</p>\n\n<p>4 7 @ J # 9 P $ L % O &copy; 5 &amp; G C W D 3 8 @ S # 1 F Y V</p>\n\n<p>If all the numbers in the above arrangement are dropped, then how many consonants are there which are immediately preceded by a symbol?</p>",
